    {
      "id": "zoom-and-wheel-behavior-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Gesture Contract Sketch",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-and-wheel-behavior"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Gesture contract (sketch)\n\nThe rules, as input by target, after Michael's decisions: zoom is about the middle of the screen, and the plain wheel zooms the camera when nothing under the pointer can scroll.\n\n## Zoom gestures\n\n| Input | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| Ctrl or Cmd + wheel | Camera zoom about the screen centre, wherever the pointer is. Page zoom is prevented. |\n| Trackpad pinch (a wheel with ctrl set) | Same as Ctrl + wheel. |\n| Ctrl or Cmd + plus | Camera zoom in one step (a factor of 1.2). |\n| Ctrl or Cmd + minus | Camera zoom out one step. |\n| Ctrl or Cmd + zero | Camera zoom back to 1. |\n| Browser-menu zoom | Cannot be intercepted. Left alone. |\n\n## The plain wheel\n\n| Pointer is over | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| A surface that can scroll in that direction | That surface scrolls. |\n| A surface whose inner region is at its end, with an outer region that can scroll | The outer region scrolls (scroll chaining). |\n| A surface at the end of its scroll, or one with nothing to scroll | The camera zooms. |\n| Empty canvas | The camera zooms. |\n| A page view drawn behind the workspace | It scrolls when it can, then the camera zooms. |\n| Embedded content the page cannot read | The frame keeps the wheel (open question). |\n| Shift + wheel | Horizontal scroll, then horizontal pan. Not built. |\n\n## Latching\n\nA gesture should belong to the surface it started on until it pauses, so a flick that reaches the end of a page does not jump to the camera partway through. Not built yet.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nTouch panning and pinch on touch screens, the zoom controls themselves, and the semantic levels that depend on zoom."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
