          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "What should browser-menu zoom do?",
        "question": "Zoom chosen from the browser menu or a keyboard shortcut the page cannot cancel scales the page anyway. Should Twilite detect the change and convert it into camera zoom (undoing the page scale), accept it as page scale and leave the camera alone, or do something in between?",
        "status": "open",
        "answer": "Open. Converting is closest to \"browser zoom zooms the camera\" but fights the browser and may break accessibility reflow. Accepting it is honest but leaves two zooms. Detect through devicePixelRatio and the visual viewport, try converting in the smallest case, and let a small trial show which one people can live with.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-question",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-question.node-class.node",
