      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "What does the plain wheel do over empty canvas?",
        "question": "Over the bare canvas, with nothing to scroll, should the plain wheel pan the camera (the web rule) or keep zooming (today, and what many canvas tools do)?",
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Answered by Michael: it zooms, about the middle of the screen. That is the most humane choice, and it is what the workspace already did. Ctrl+wheel therefore adds nothing new, except that it is now always camera zoom, never browser page zoom. Panning with the wheel is not part of the contract.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
        "_classBinding": {
