      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "How long does a wheel gesture stay with its surface?",
        "question": "When a flick starts on a scrollable surface and reaches its end, the rest of the flick should not jump to the camera. How long a pause ends the gesture, and how does it differ for a wheel, a trackpad with momentum, and touch?",
        "status": "open",
        "answer": "Open. Browsers use a short idle timeout (on the order of a couple hundred milliseconds). Start with the same and tune it on a trackpad with momentum, which is where mid-gesture handoff is most visible.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
