      "data": {
        "title": "How are cross-origin frames handled?",
        "question": "A cross-origin frame keeps its own wheel handling and cannot be inspected. What is the least surprising rule at its edges, and does the camera still get a way to move while the pointer is over it?",
        "status": "open",
        "answer": "Open. PersistentIframe already treats same-origin frames as canvas-first and leaves cross-origin frames alone. Likely rule: the frame owns the wheel while the pointer is inside it, and the camera can still be moved with a modifier or by the frame edge. Check against the frames Twilite actually hosts.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
        "_classBinding": {
