      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "The first test bench run: 4 of 8 cases match the contract",
        "observation": "The bench (github://mikemartinez1974/public/qa/wheel-test-bench/root.node) was run in the app with its check script. Over a scrollable surface the surface keeps the wheel, including a nested scroller at both ends (cases 1 to 4 match). Cases 5 to 8 do not. Over a content node at the end of its scroll, or with nothing to scroll, the wheel goes nowhere: the node listener stops the event before the canvas handler sees it, so the camera cannot be moved with the wheel from there. On empty canvas the plain wheel zooms, and it zooms about the middle of the screen, not the pointer. Ctrl and wheel is treated as a plain wheel, zooming about the screen centre with the point under the pointer moving by hundreds of pixels. This also shows that the arbiter is only reached by wheel events that are not over a node.",
        "kind": "experiment",
        "strength": "strong",
        "definitionKey": "idea-evidence",
        "_classBinding": {
